{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm working out the bit mapping: underline2 sits at bit 9 and the map has 13 entries, so adding double_underline as bit 13 is the cleanest option. That means extending the `_style_map` range and widening the bit mask to cover bits 9 through 13.\n\nI'm weighing whether double_underline should share bit 9 with underline2, since both emit SGR 21, or take its own bit 13. A shared bit would make the two properties identical, which might be sensible, but a separate bit keeps existing behavior untouched, so I'm leaning toward that and checking what else enumerates the bits.\n\nI'm weighing whether double_underline should reuse underline2's SGR 21 or get its own bit, since sharing would be simpler but a separate bit leaves existing behavior alone. I'm leaning toward a separate bit 13 with \"double_underline\" as the canonical string, while keeping parsing aliases for the variants.\n\nI still need to confirm that the hyphenated \"double-underline\" name parses inside markup tags, so I'm checking the markup regex and how console.py exports the SVG.\n\n","thinkingSignature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1oYWlrdS01LjUtMjAyNjEwMDd8Y2xhdWRlLW9uLWF3cyJ9"},{"type":"text","text":"The existing `underline2` uses bit 9 (SGR 21), and the bit-group masks are hardcoded. I'll add `double_underline` as a new bit 13 so existing `underline2` behavior stays unchanged. Next I'll check the SVG export and the markup tag regex."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_018ZJwL6Px1ZSy7GNauSsScS","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /app && sed -n 2380,2420p rich/console.py; grep -n \"RE_TAGS\\|re.compile\" -A8 rich/markup.py | head -30; grep -rn \"underline\" tests/*.py | head -40"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"openrouter","model":"anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5","usage":{"input":2,"output":1188,"cacheRead":6601,"cacheWrite":9641,"totalTokens":17432,"cost":{"input":2.0000000000000002e-7,"