{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":2,"output":596,"cacheRead":50575,"cacheWrite":229,"totalTokens":51402,"cost":{"input":2.0000000000000002e-7,"output":0.000298,"cacheRead":0.00050575,"cacheWrite":0.000028625,"total":0.000832575,"totalFromProvider":true},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":0},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"`double_underline` is now a first-class style attribute in Rich, and it exports to HTML and SVG. The full suite shows the same 12 failures before and after my change (all in `test_syntax.py` and related), so nothing regressed. The new tests pass.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- **`rich/style.py`**\n  - `Style(double_underline=True)` is accepted, and `.double_underline` is a boolean property.\n  - `double_underline`, `double-underline`, and `du` parse in style strings and markup, including `not du`.\n  - It is stored as a new bit (13), so `underline2` and its `uu` alias are untouched.\n  - ANSI output is SGR `21`, e.g. `[du red]x[/]` renders as `\\x1b[21;31mx\\x1b[0m`.\n  - `str()` and `__rich_repr__` include it, and `style1 + style2` and `Style.combine()` preserve it.\n  - `get_html_style()` emits `text-decoration: underline double`. When both `underline` and `double_underline` are set, the double rule wins.\n- **`rich/console.py`**: `export_svg()` emits `text-decoration: underline double;` for double-underlined styles.\n- **`tests/test_style.py`**: three new tests covering parsing, combining, ANSI, and HTML output.\n\n**Notes**\n\n- Rich already had `underline2`, which also emits SGR 21 but never produced CSS. I left it alone. If you want `underline2` to export the same CSS, that's a one-line change in each exporter.\n- The working tree already had `.ki-base/*` files deleted before I started. I did not touch them.\n- mypy isn't installed in this environment, so I did not run the type check that `AGENTS.md` asks for. The new code uses the same annotated patterns as the existing attributes."}}
