haracter, it is converted to two spaces.\nrich/cells.py:284:    If the cell position falls within a double width character, it is converted to two spaces.\nrich/panel.py:305:    from .box import DOUBLE, ROUNDED\nrich/panel.py:312:        box=DOUBLE,\nrich/segment.py:111:        Note that splitting a double-width character, may result in that character turning\nrich/style.py:59:        underline2 (bool, optional): Enable doubly underlined text. Defaults to None.\nrich/style.py:123:        \"underline2\": \"underline2\",\nrich/style.py:124:        \"uu\": \"underline2\",\nrich/style.py:145:        underline2: Optional[bool] = None,\nrich/style.py:171:                underline2 is not None and 512,\nrich/style.py:189:                    underline2 and 512 or 0,\nrich/style.py:284:    underline2 = _Bit(9)\nrich/style.py:322:                    append(\"underline2\" if self.underline2 else \"not underline2\")\nrich/style.py:424:        yield \"underline2\", self.underline2, None\nrich/traceback.py:121:        locals_hide_dunder (bool, optional): Hide locals prefixed with double underscore. Defaults to True.\nrich/traceback.py:279:        locals_hide_dunder (bool, optional): Hide locals prefixed with double underscore. Defaults to True.\nrich/traceback.py:392:            locals_hide_dunder (bool, optional): Hide locals prefixed with double underscore. Defaults to True.\nrich/traceback.py:458:            locals_hide_dunder (bool, optional): Hide locals prefixed with double underscore. Defaults to True.\nrich/tree.py:106:                guide = 1 if style.bold else (2 if style.underline2 else 0)\nrich/tree.py:115:        remove_guide_styles = Style(bold=False, underline2=False)\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":3790,"timestamp":1794167243981},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There's already an `underline2` attribute to deal with, and the job is to add `double_underline` as a new name. I'll go through style.py in full to see how it's set up.\n\n"